# OPD reference (BRIEF_to_opd_reference, Dave 2026-10-10): the CHIEF ray is the default,
# the aperture MEAN the option -- per session (OPDREF), per deck (UseChfRay4OPD= N).
# Every OPD run prints which it used.  The pre-fix engine prints no such line, and
# reads 'opdref' as OPD (LCMP prefix match on 'OPD',3): red on it.
# The printed RMS / P-V / 'Average OPD' do not depend on the reference (RMS and P-V
# are mean-removed; 'Average OPD' is DAvgl, the mean of ray-minus-chief OPL, which
# is the constant the two maps differ by), so they are asserted unchanged.
old $ROOT/docs/macos-manual/examples/Cassegrain.in
opd 5
/null
opdref mean
opd 5
opdref
chief
opd 5
old $ROOT/ZGD_test_files/tst_opdref_mean.in
opd 5
opdref chief
old $ROOT/ZGD_test_files/tst_opdref_mean.in
opd 5
opdref mean
old $ROOT/docs/macos-manual/examples/Cassegrain.in
opd 5
# EXPECT: OPD reference: CHIEF RAY \(default\)\s*\n RMS OPD error is\s+1\.29\d+D-12
# EXPECT: OPD reference \(CHIEF,MEAN\): \[CHIEF\]: mean
# EXPECT: APERTURE MEAN \(opt-in; the chief ray is the default\)
# EXPECT: OPD reference: APERTURE MEAN \(OPDREF MEAN\)\s*\n RMS OPD error is\s+1\.29\d+D-12
# EXPECT: OPD reference \(CHIEF,MEAN\): \[MEAN\]: chief
# EXPECT: OPD reference: CHIEF RAY \(OPDREF CHIEF\)
# EXPECT: OPD reference: APERTURE MEAN \(UseChfRay4OPD= N\)
# the session option survives a plain load (rule 6: not reset per load)
# EXPECT: Cassegrain\.in\s+being loaded\.[\s\S]*OPD reference: APERTURE MEAN \(OPDREF MEAN\)\s*\n RMS[\s\S]*\Z
# EXPECT: Average OPD is\s+-?\d\.\d+D-(1\d|[2-9]\d)
# EXPECT-NOT: Average OPD is\s+(?=\S)(?!-?\d\.\d+D-(1\d|[2-9]\d))
